    "---\n",
    "# Section 9 — Conclusion\n",
    "\n",
    "## Summary of Findings\n",
    "\n",
    "This project applied machine learning to predict depression among students using a single dataset covering academic, lifestyle, and demographic factors.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Model Performance (Test Set — 5,581 students)\n",
    "\n",
    "| Model | Accuracy | F1-Score | ROC-AUC |\n",
    "|---|---|---|---|\n",
    "| **Random Forest** ⭐ | **~83.9%** | **~0.863** | **~0.916** |\n",
    "| Decision Tree | ~81.8% | ~0.841 | ~0.868 |\n",
    "| Logistic Regression | ~83.9% | ~0.860 | ~0.917 |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Key Findings\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Random Forest** was selected as the primary model due to its ensemble design, robustness to overfitting, and ability to produce feature importance scores — directly supporting the project objective of identifying key predictors.\n",
    "\n",
    "2. **Top 3 depression predictors** (by feature importance):\n",
    "   - Suicidal Thoughts history (strongest signal)\n",
    "   - Academic Pressure (confirms the academic stress hypothesis)\n",
    "   - Financial Stress (economic factors matter significantly)\n",
    "\n",
    "3. A ROC-AUC of ~0.916 indicates the model correctly distinguishes depressed from non-depressed students 91.6% of the time — well above random chance (0.50).\n",
    "\n",
    "### Limitations\n",
    "\n",
    "- The dataset is self-reported and may contain response bias.\n",
    "- The model predicts a binary outcome and cannot capture severity or nuance.\n",
    "- Results should not be used for clinical diagnosis.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Recommendations\n",
    "\n",
    "- Universities should monitor academic pressure and financial stress as early warning signs.\n",
    "- Counselling services should be proactively offered to students showing these risk factors.\n",
    "- Future work could explore time-series data or real-time monitoring systems.\n",
